<title>USA: GM March U.S. car sales rise.</title>
<headline>GM March U.S. car sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp</p>
<p>			Mar 1-31, 1997     Mar 1-31, 1996 *Pct Chng</p>
<p> Total Car		244,352	   243,462	     +0.4</p>
<p> Total Truck	    190,446	   174,330	     +9.2</p>
<p> Total Vehicle	  434,798	   417,792	     +4.1</p>
<p>		  Jan 1-Mar 31, 1997 Jan 1-Mar 31, 1996 *Pct Chng</p>
<p> Total Car		638,953	   661,081	     -2.1</p>
<p> Total Truck	    483,969	   491,052	     -0.1</p>
<p> Total Vehicle	1,122,922	 1,152,133	     -1.3</p>
<p>* Pct change based on daily selling rate. Sale days 26 in latest month vs 26, 76 for year to date vs 77 in year ago.</p>
<p>NOTE: Total GM car sales include U.S. sales figures from Saab Automobile AB, which is 50 percent owned by GM and 50 percent owned by Sweden's AB Investor. Saab's U.S. sales in March totaled 1,993 cars, down from 2,464 in March 1996.</p>
</text>
